# Testing

Follow `.specify/memory/constitution.md` section III and the Definition of Done.

- Write the failing Pest test before the behavior it locks.
- Feature tests live in `tests/Feature/Modules/{Module}` and call the real HTTP stack. Do not mock the Action or Service that implements the endpoint.
- Unit tests live in `tests/Unit/Modules/{Module}` and cover branches one HTTP call cannot reach.
- Fake outbound HTTP, storage, cache, mail, queues, and notifications. Use the test database; do not mock Eloquent to skip a migration this feature owns.
- Frontend tests live under `resources/js/**/__tests__` or `*.spec.ts`.

Prove a change with `make test` for the suites it touches, and `make verify` before the work is done. `make verify` runs formatter checks, Larastan, deptrac, the production Vue build, Pest, and Vitest. It checks formatting and does not rewrite files. A PHP-only change may use `php artisan test --compact tests/Feature/Modules/<Module>/<Test>.php` while iterating, then `make verify`.
